# --- Added 2026-09-24 (second pass) ------------------------------------------
# private.finance_post_voucher_redeemed had two bugs, found while auditing
# whether promo-code/care-voucher-covered service purchases report accurately
# on the finance dashboard (20260924211113_fix_voucher_redemption_finance_
# posting_amount_and_deferral.sql): it always posted the voucher's full
# face_value_kobo as revenue instead of the amount actually applied to the
# order (redeem_care_voucher's own least(face_value_kobo, payable)), and for a
# service_purchase it always posted straight to 4100 immediate revenue with no
# check for service_products.access_duration_days -- the same bounded-duration
# pack paid by card or platform credit correctly defers to 2000 with a
# recognition schedule. Proves a reward voucher worth more than a bounded-
# duration order's price posts only the covered amount, deferred to 2000, with
# a correctly-sized 4020 recognition schedule; a control proves the same for an
# unbounded order (covered amount, straight to 4100, no schedule); sabotage
# reverts the trigger to the pre-fix unconditional-face-value/unconditional-
# 4100 body and confirms both holes reopen on a fresh redemption.
voucher_redemption_finance_posting_amount_and_deferral.sql

# --- Added 2026-09-24 (third pass) -------------------------------------------
# public.finance_revenue_by_funding_source() (20260924211136_finance_revenue_
# by_funding_source.sql) is a new read-side dashboard RPC, not a bug fix, but
# gets the same standing-regression treatment given the financial-correctness
# stakes: a reward-voucher-funded bounded-duration purchase's recognised
# revenue must land entirely in promotional_minor, a platform-credit-paid_
# balance-funded one entirely in cash_minor, a plain card payment/voucher
# redemption classified correctly at the point-of-sale leg, and nothing in
# unclassified_minor. Sabotage collapses the function back to summing every
# revenue-account credit as cash (the pre-fix gap: no funding-source
# distinction at all) and confirms the split disappears, proving the checks
# discriminate rather than passing vacuously.
finance_revenue_by_funding_source.sql

# --- Added 2026-09-24 (fourth pass) -------------------------------------------
# /code-review high on the previous two migrations, before they were ever
# merged, found two real bugs the fix pass above introduced: private.
# finance_post_voucher_redeemed read the redeeming order's voucher_covered_kobo,
# which is CUMULATIVE across every voucher ever applied to that order, so a
# second voucher redeemed directly against an already-partially-covered order
# (redeem_care_voucher has no "one discount per order" guard of its own -- that
# lives one layer up, in redeem_promo_code) double-counted the first voucher's
# amount; and finance_revenue_by_funding_source computed one blended cash/promo
# ratio per service_purchase and applied it to every revenue_recognition_
# schedules row tied to that purchase, even though a single purchase can
# accumulate multiple, separately-funded schedules (a partial voucher plus a
# later card/platform-credit remainder) -- correct over the purchase's full
# lifetime, wrong for any single reporting period queried before all of a
# purchase's schedules have posted revenue. Fixed at the root
# (20260924213634_fix_voucher_redemption_cross_voucher_double_count_and_revrec_
# rounding.sql) by persisting the exact per-voucher covered amount and the
# exact per-schedule promotional split at the moment each is created, instead
# of re-deriving either from state shared with other redemptions/schedules.
# Proves a second voucher against an already-partially-covered order posts
# only its own amount; a purchase with two separately-funded schedules reports
# a mid-period recognition of only one as fully attributed, not blended with
# the other's lifetime share; the original single-schedule fix still holds;
# and two independent sabotage steps (reverting each trigger to its pre-fix
# shape) reopen the corresponding hole.
voucher_redemption_cross_voucher_double_count_and_revrec_rounding.sql

# --- Added 2026-09-24 (fifth pass) --------------------------------------------
# 20260924213634 above added a 10th parameter to private.finance_create_
# recognition_schedule via `create or replace function` — which only replaces
# a function with an IDENTICAL parameter list, so Postgres created a SECOND
# overload instead of replacing the original. Every existing 9-argument call
# site (finance_post_from_payment, finance_post_platform_credit_ledger_entry,
# finance_post_voucher_redeemed) became ambiguous (42725) and, because those
# callers run inside an exception-swallowing handler built to protect a
# payment webhook from an accounting failure, the ambiguity was silently
# recorded into finance_posting_failures instead of raised: every booking/
# subscription/add_on/service_purchase payment landed with ZERO GL entries and
# ZERO revenue recognition schedules. Found live (koiplnmbgnqnbywhpjlf) while
# testing an unrelated PR, confirmed no real production transaction was caught
# in the window, fixed by dropping the original 9-argument overload
# (20260924221152_fix_finance_create_recognition_schedule_overload_ambiguity.sql).
# Proves exactly one overload exists, a real 9-argument call site (a
# bounded-duration service_purchase payment) posts cleanly, and sabotage
# (recreating the dropped overload) reproduces the exact 42725 ambiguity.
finance_create_recognition_schedule_overload_ambiguity.sql

